This helper is meant to run at most 3 tasks at a time. Each task returns a promise and takes a different, random amount of time. With 10 tasks and `limit = 3`, how many can end up running at once?

```js
async function pool(tasks, limit) {
  const results = [];
  const running = [];
  for (const task of tasks) {
    const p = task().then((r) => results.push(r));
    running.push(p);
    if (running.length >= limit) await Promise.race(running);
  }
  await Promise.all(running);
  return results;
}
```

