`fn` is an async function that rejects the first two times it is called and succeeds on the third. What does `await retry(fn)` do?

```js
const sleep = (ms) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));
async function retry(fn, attempts = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i < attempts; i++) {
    try {
      return fn();
    } catch (err) {
      if (i === attempts - 1) throw err;
      await sleep(2 ** i * 100);
    }
  }
}
```

